<section class="section" id="discovery">
  <div class="container">
    <p class="eyebrow">Step 3: point it at the unknown</p>
    <h2>25 real, unconfirmed TESS candidates</h2>
    <p>
      Same pipeline, real TESS Objects of Interest still flagged as planet candidates by the archive, nobody has
      fully verified these yet. For each one: download the light curve, detrend, run this pipeline's own BLS
      search bounded around the catalog's reported period, an independent check rather than just trusting the
      catalog value, then physically characterize whatever depth is used.
    </p>

    <div class="summary-row">
      <div class="card summary-card">
        <div class="summary-num">25<span class="summary-den">/25</span></div>
        <div class="summary-label">candidates characterized</div>
      </div>
      <div class="card summary-card">
        <div class="summary-num">16<span class="summary-den">/25</span></div>
        <div class="summary-label">independently re-detected by this pipeline's own BLS, within 1%</div>
      </div>
    </div>

    <p>
      Every candidate in this batch (all under 15-day orbital periods) comes back too hot for its star's
      habitable zone, physically expected: short orbital periods mean small semi-major axes. Full table with
      per-candidate radius, orbital distance, and equilibrium temperature (each with a Monte Carlo uncertainty
      range, not a single precise-looking number):
      <a href="https://github.com/AmjadAAYD/exoplanet-transit-detection/blob/main/docs/discovery_table.csv">discovery_table.csv</a>.
    </p>

    <div class="caveat">
      <strong>None of these are confirmed planets.</strong> This pipeline flags transit-like signals, it does not
      confirm them. Real confirmation needs follow-up spectroscopy or radial-velocity data outside the scope of
      this project, the same first step real discovery pipelines take, not a discovery in itself.
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

<style>
  .summary-row {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: repeat(2, 1fr);
    gap: 16px;
    margin: 32px 0 28px;
  }
  .summary-card { text-align: center; }
  .summary-num {
    font-size: 2.4rem;
    font-weight: 700;
    color: var(--accent-2);
    font-variant-numeric: tabular-nums;
  }
  .summary-den { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 1.4rem; }
  .summary-label { color: var(--text-dim); font-size: 0.9rem; margin-top: 4px; }

  @media (max-width: 640px) {
    .summary-row { grid-template-columns: 1fr; }
  }
</style>
